{"title":"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 20","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1.1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1.1</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Operation_Descartes)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Operation Descartes)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(When_You&#39;re_Running_Out_of_Time)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (When You're Running Out of Time)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Isosceles triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/81366638e694deb1959c886bb89a07f71eff44a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T&#39;$\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are not congruent but have the same area and the same perimeter.  The sides of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> have lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, while those of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/81366638e694deb1959c886bb89a07f71eff44a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T&#39;$\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> have lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />.  Which of the following numbers is closest to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/d/98d79a2d96c752228f16d39016128a3b90b05436.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }3\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }4\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }5\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }6\\qquad\\textbf{(E) }8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"353\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/3/6d3908bb6568001af287bff3d6b420a82367f6da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{2} \\cdot 8 \\cdot 3 = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"99\" height=\"37\" /> and the perimeter is 18.\n</p><p>The area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/81366638e694deb1959c886bb89a07f71eff44a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T&#39;$\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/c/c6c7ade345e239cecdc3a830ef7966aae353c3aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{2} b \\sqrt{a^2 - (\\dfrac{b}{2})^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"112\" height=\"43\" /> and the perimeter is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/f/a3f62722cb258211df52beca5271d3f7130ee1fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a + b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/8/a285ac163c84282bb1f65f43db5286edec2d6551.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a + b = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"93\" height=\"16\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/9/109f1ef7a81c7df5cab0138d634daf784a9cf772.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a = 18 - b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"93\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/a/b1a34d74db29437f74d18085ff99f0088deca74f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12 = \\dfrac{1}{2} b \\sqrt{a^2 - (\\dfrac{b}{2})^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"155\" height=\"43\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/4/824417fa6c08bac0758f0146d7f4a5dcb7070a99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$48 = b \\sqrt{4a^2 - b^2} = b \\sqrt{(18 - b)^2 - b^2} = b \\sqrt{324 - 36b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"409\" height=\"32\" />.\n</p><p>We square and divide 36 from both sides to obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/a/bca40791ca2e4a39a84e1bc4daabe4f3da0ffe3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$64 = b^2 (9 - b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"19\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/9/dd9174b74554fe287ebf2d7583a5806ed7d0e171.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^3 - 9b^2 + 64 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"135\" height=\"16\" />. Since we know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/4/0b447277e683dbf98cb0cbcbddf0debfd717e1c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 8$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> is a solution, we divide by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/d/96d6d95c2e9ed89c3a7618cea76308c041d793cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b - 8$\" width=\"38\" height=\"12\" /> to get the other solution. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/7/d370a0645abe2af2116a2b2b3eaa4fdfbc7febf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^2 - b - 8 = 0$\" width=\"109\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/d/bcde2537337dcbdd69ee8c3d8dd54db4a0737c13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = \\dfrac{1 + \\sqrt{33}}{2} &lt; \\dfrac{1 + 6}{2} = 3.5.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"220\" height=\"41\" /> The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/b/26b24dfda9c973a310d9a971b5ec21834e73f10d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"56\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1.1\">Solution 1.1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1.1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, the semiperimeter is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/0/2704c86dbc040d3d9fa78d765cf9574cad77470c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 9 - \\frac12b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"86\" height=\"37\" />. Using Heron's formula, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/6/db6c913dcb9526ed029384cad9ab6dff0e633aed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{9\\left(\\frac{b}{2}\\right)\\left(\\frac{b}{2}\\right)(9-b)} = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"209\" height=\"53\" />. Squaring both sides and simplifying, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/e/62e2f8c391948a4335f19dde426f3da20d78e191.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-b^3+9b^2-64=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"149\" height=\"16\" />. Since we know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/4/0b447277e683dbf98cb0cbcbddf0debfd717e1c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 8$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> is a solution, we divide by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/d/96d6d95c2e9ed89c3a7618cea76308c041d793cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b - 8$\" width=\"38\" height=\"12\" /> to get the other solution. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/7/d370a0645abe2af2116a2b2b3eaa4fdfbc7febf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^2 - b - 8 = 0$\" width=\"109\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/d/bcde2537337dcbdd69ee8c3d8dd54db4a0737c13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = \\dfrac{1 + \\sqrt{33}}{2} &lt; \\dfrac{1 + 6}{2} = 3.5.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"220\" height=\"41\" /> The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/b/26b24dfda9c973a310d9a971b5ec21834e73f10d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"56\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, being isosceles, has an area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/3/4c3770a98a005e5e16663fbead85d5e23d3c54b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}(8)\\sqrt{5^2-4^2}=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"148\" height=\"37\" /> and a perimeter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/3/c2312b9ca68dd42131241ca63d9c6b73ef03991e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5+5+8=18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"113\" height=\"14\" />.\nTriangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/81366638e694deb1959c886bb89a07f71eff44a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T&#39;$\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> similarly has an area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/b/99b22e0843e4becc44d782c604461595b78e9bbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}(b)\\bigg(\\sqrt{a^2-\\frac{b^2}{4}}\\bigg)=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"179\" height=\"46\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/8/fd8d913950dc6bb52df4a68019053c4e79be030a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a+b=18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"90\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Now we apply our computational fortitude.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/4/404f5910ccf93200c3b4bde321a1586da4a749d6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2}(b)\\bigg(\\sqrt{a^2-\\frac{b^2}{4}}\\bigg)=12\\]\" width=\"177\" height=\"46\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/c/6aca1ba6b0c4299631fcf4a8c25c32df78a52439.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(b)\\bigg(\\sqrt{a^2-\\frac{b^2}{4}}\\bigg)=24\\]\" width=\"165\" height=\"46\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/d/c2d329c7a0953ecd5c62309eb774cc215b5d576e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(b)\\sqrt{4a^2-b^2}=48\\]\" width=\"141\" height=\"21\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/7/fb7a226c5903b1b6fcf63279d9f7f1a6598fd3cf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[b^2(4a^2-b^2)=48^2\\]\" width=\"141\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/7/9a70abc0c3b5c4afa3f8726d5ea9070a2053ad45.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[b^2(2a+b)(2a-b)=48^2\\]\" width=\"188\" height=\"19\" />\nPlug in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/8/fd8d913950dc6bb52df4a68019053c4e79be030a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a+b=18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"90\" height=\"14\" /> to obtain\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/2/4423d55d0ee00e5d352e2f78639c7c35fcf659cd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[18b^2(2a-b)=48^2\\]\" width=\"143\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/0/fa02f276c9a2a901830d31b484e1c085475f3fb7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[b^2(2a-b)=128\\]\" width=\"128\" height=\"19\" />\nPlug in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/4/4a4bbf32d4a3994c6685b528bf94ec17ab8412f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a=18-b$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"91\" height=\"13\" /> to obtain\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/0/060d612ce581dcf65e26a38729d2406060adf449.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[b^2(18-2b)=128\\]\" width=\"137\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/0/d4081941bec5feb1777ce36299433556df4a6e34.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2b^3-18b^2+128=0\\]\" width=\"162\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/b/19b04fbeca159dd86c318ef81b24755b2da3f38b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[b^3-9b^2+64=0\\]\" width=\"134\" height=\"16\" />\nWe know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/c/b2ccc9e3c02a4b38f185d5b43a4b7456338e30a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=8$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> is a valid solution by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. Factoring out <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/e/a1e02d0c9d01c03e32236923457c82f2f61e938f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b-8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />, we obtain\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/4/2e4792223535e4ce3480ab4f27b923ccf53bf2f3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(b-8)(b^2-b-8)=0 \\Rightarrow b^2-b-8=0\\]\" width=\"313\" height=\"19\" />\nUtilizing the quadratic formula gives\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/9/239db30bdd7a28217f6c751326d20b2c826cbaaa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[b=\\frac{1\\pm\\sqrt{33}}{2}\\]\" width=\"98\" height=\"41\" />\nWe clearly must pick the positive solution. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/e/23e1ebfb51058abfa58d8b0de94faab9840b40f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5&lt;\\sqrt{33}&lt;6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"99\" height=\"18\" />, and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/e/a1ed9a6e1ae0b2873b2c1c77480a29703cc2600b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${3&lt;\\frac{1+\\sqrt{33}}{2}&lt;\\frac{7}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"141\" height=\"43\" />, which clearly gives an answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/b/26b24dfda9c973a310d9a971b5ec21834e73f10d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"56\" height=\"28\" />, as desired.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Triangle T has perimeter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/1/54170a459de7dd548185741a0848c81252639d8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 + 5 + 8 = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"113\" height=\"14\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/3/5a3c4d0aae88771fb64acb0a012f086f16502829.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18 = 2a + b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"91\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Using Heron's, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/1/de1e58816486231a29401698cc8fce4127489523.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{(9)(4)^2(1)} = \\sqrt{(\\frac{2a+b}{2})\\left(\\frac{b}{2}\\right)^2(\\frac{2a-b}{2})}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"323\" height=\"53\" />.\n</p><p>We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/8/a285ac163c84282bb1f65f43db5286edec2d6551.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a + b = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"93\" height=\"16\" /> from above so we plug that in, and we also know that then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/a/ffabb821556de6002e92721f5bf519815fdc0c3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a - b = 18 - 2b$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"130\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/3/e435beb2a9deae97e0567fd82e64a891294b48f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12 = \\frac{3b}{2}\\sqrt{9-b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"118\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/0/98073a0d344921606c532e4eee3320f3a2839377.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$64 = 9b^2 - b^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>We plug in 3 for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> in the LHS, and we get 54 which is too low. We plug in 4 for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> in the LHS, and we get 80 which is too high. We now know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is some number between 3 and 4. \n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/4/be4c0d27fc46f001a301b2873c290c638c7f88d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b \\geq 3.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"54\" height=\"15\" />, then we would round up to 4, but if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/c/adc6304379943e9adb199e67a25cbbf19cfc3440.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b &lt; 3.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"57\" height=\"15\" />, then we would round down to 3. So let us plug in 3.5 for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>We get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/5/6f5beac1486d8b43f365cc7215f1d00c7b435fbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$67.375$\" width=\"49\" height=\"12\" /> which is too high, so we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/c/adc6304379943e9adb199e67a25cbbf19cfc3440.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b &lt; 3.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"57\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Thus the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/b/26b24dfda9c973a310d9a971b5ec21834e73f10d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"56\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Operation_Descartes.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Operation_Descartes)\">Solution 4 (Operation Descartes)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Operation Descartes)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For this new triangle, say its legs have length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and the base length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/6/9f6072f36e4577a20084d5e518bf7e2f2068ab3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2c$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />. To see why I did this, draw the triangle on a Cartesian plane where the altitude is part of the y-axis! Then, we notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/c/c9cf8b02cccfb7a6694a2d3ded933ee3137f3bc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c+d=9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/a/0aac866a23b86d0fac84399c7bbf3927b26f6eff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c*\\sqrt{d^2-c^2}=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"136\" height=\"18\" />. It's better to let a side be some variable so we avoid having to add non-square roots and square-roots!!\n</p><p>Now, modify the square-root equation with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/6/366ee86fb411653ffa5eeb259cbdec408cf4c8b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=9-c$\" width=\"73\" height=\"12\" />; you get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/c/cccafa59adc5e1b3b16b22f810b62ce9c663a88a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c^2*(81-18c)=144$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"164\" height=\"19\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/6/3c64bd5c77bed9947ed6a57bef8ec57979c23217.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-18c^3+81c^2=144$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"154\" height=\"16\" />. Divide by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/8/a483ee25b066703890405f0127fef9c31572fb81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/3/d93f957aa15f7cbf8a31b3a0a8c2fa408b58c03b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2c^3-9c^2+16=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"144\" height=\"16\" />. Obviously, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/3/c63e18205b2a13c9f8d283e834e0bb8d145ba305.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" /> is a root as established by triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />! So, use synthetic division to obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/0/a50f7ac7ef292d812e71ceccf0d0807f622ab72d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2c^2-c-4=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"121\" height=\"18\" />, upon which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/5/7d57a25596fc958b6706692b6e146dac806c3e11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=\\frac{1+\\sqrt{33}}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"99\" height=\"41\" />, which is closest to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/d/cfdbd19877c13d1755e01b54ba640f512c883a34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> (as opposed to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />). That's enough to confirm that the answer has to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/b/26b24dfda9c973a310d9a971b5ec21834e73f10d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"56\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28When_You.27re_Running_Out_of_Time.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(When_You're_Running_Out_of_Time)\">Solution 5 (When You're Running Out of Time)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (When You&#39;re Running Out of Time)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/81366638e694deb1959c886bb89a07f71eff44a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T&#39;$\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> have the same area and the same perimeter,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/8/fd8d913950dc6bb52df4a68019053c4e79be030a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a+b=18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"90\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/a/b7ace9ef90585b4a9997dcd14b475182111f2d82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9*(9-a)^2(9-b) = 9*4^2*1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"234\" height=\"19\" />\nBy trying each answer choice, it is clear that the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/b/26b24dfda9c973a310d9a971b5ec21834e73f10d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"56\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A\">2015 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017235842\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.048 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.060 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 608/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1963/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 18214/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.549      1 Template:AMC12_box\n100.00%    7.549      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:13965:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017235842 and revision id 155556. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}